  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-purpose Cash Response for Food Insecure Households impacted by Drought</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian context in drought-affected areas of southern and eastern Ethiopia is quickly changing, and the gravity of the situation today has already surpassed the ongoing response. A further scale-up of the humanitarian response is required across sectors to meet the increasing needs of the most vulnerable populations facing dire needs in large parts of southern and eastern Ethiopia. Large areas of Oromia and Somali regions, parts of Southern Nations, Nationalities, and People&apos;s region, and Southwest Ethiopia Peoples&apos; region are highly affected by the drought. Dramatic increases in food insecurity, malnutrition, displacement, as well as deteriorating health and protection indices are some of the indicators of the dire humanitarian situation.Through this allocation, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is supporting support government-led efforts to address the protection and urgent needs of refugees, returning Ethiopian migrants and third country nationals fleeing the conflict in Sudan in the affected regions in Ethiopia. IOM&#x2019;s multi-sector emergency assistance will benefit 32,000 individuals, including with transportation assistance to safety, protection assistance at points of entries, emergency water, sanitation and hygiene, multi-purpose cash, and health assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
